# UP6b (R-UP12, protocol/02 invariant 6 "Withdrawal"): every member of a call drops at once and
# comes back. The room sweep issues three absence Removes, and each member's queue holds the Remove
# of its own leaf, which OpenMLS refuses to commit: before the withdrawal nobody could commit. The
# first device back resumes and withdraws its own Remove (only its own), commits the other two, and
# the other two, refused at their start (E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT), join afresh by external commit: the
# Removes are committed, so there is no freeze and no E_REMOVE_PENDING. All three end in the same
# call, and a rotation after they are back succeeds.
instance dilla
client alice
client bob
client carol
group call kind=call target=e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6e6 community=none creator=alice
join bob call via=external
sync alice
join carol call via=external
sync alice
sync bob
absent alice call
absent bob call
absent carol call
sync alice
sync bob
sync carol
resume alice call withdrawn=1
sync alice
commit alice call
expect_reject E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT resume bob call
resync bob call
expect_reject E_LEAF_NOT_CURRENT resume carol call
resync carol call
sync alice
sync bob
sync carol
commit bob call
sync alice
sync carol
send alice call all three are back
expect_decrypts bob call all three are back
expect_decrypts carol call all three are back
